::MCQ::
What are the five logging levels in Python's logging module?
{
~ major, minor, critical, warning, info
= debug, info, warning, error, critical
~ high, medium, low, error, fatal
~ trace, debug, info, warn, error
}

::MCQ::
What method is used to configure the root logger?
{
~ logging.configure()
~ logging.setup()
~ logging.init()
= logging.basicConfig()
}

::MCQ::
How do you create a custom logger in Python?
{
~ logging.create_logger()
~ logging.Logger()
= logging.getLogger(name)
~ logging.new_logger()
}

::MCQ::
What is the purpose of a Handler in logging?
{
~ To create log messages
= To send logs to specific destinations
~ To delete log files
~ To encrypt log data
}

::MCQ::
What does the 'filemode' parameter in basicConfig() do?
{
= Determines how logs are saved to a file
~ Deletes existing log files
~ Compresses log files
~ Creates a new file
}
